From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: type $ on the Q25 currency key

The Q25 keyboard sends scan code 41 (GRAVE) for its $ key and the
keychar map had no entry for it, so apps and keyboards fell back to
'`'. Map GRAVE to the printed '$' (plain, Shift and Caps Lock).
Other keys and the Alt layer are unchanged.
---
 configs/keychars/Q25_keyboard.kcm | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configs/keychars/Q25_keyboard.kcm b/configs/keychars/Q25_keyboard.kcm
index 5196c3b..3bd6d8e 100644
--- a/configs/keychars/Q25_keyboard.kcm
+++ b/configs/keychars/Q25_keyboard.kcm
@@ -265,3 +265,12 @@ key 0 {
     alt:                                '0'
     shift+alt:                          '0'
 }
+
+# SableOS: the currency key (printed $) sends scan code 41, GRAVE, which had
+# no entry here, so keyboards typed '`' or nothing. Type the printed '$' in
+# every app and keyboard; Alt+$ is left to the app (Sable Keyboard keeps '$').
+key GRAVE {
+    label:                              '$'
+    base:                               '$'
+    shift, capslock:                    '$'
+}
